{
	"name": "Caustic Sap",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/acid/dissolve-drip-droplet-smoke.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Starting at 10th level, when you hit a creature with your Sanguine Transference that is immune to poison, treat its immunity as resistance instead.</p><p>Additionally, so long as you are not at your full hit point total, any creature who hits you with a natural weapon (such as claws or a bite) or attempts to grapple you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw versus your maneuver DC. On a success, they take 2d4 acid damage and nothing further happens. On a failure, the creature takes the acid damage but also takes 1d4 ongoing acid damage. A creature may end this ongoing damage if they use an action to wipe the acid away. You may use this ability a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier per long rest.</p>",
